WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:08.297
This is Karya for students. Major projects, minor projects, hackathons. Let's set up a hackathon project, with a team, from scratch.

2
00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:14.228
Choose I'm a student, and create a free account. That's all it takes.

3
00:00:16.239 --> 00:00:23.157
Pick what you're working on. Major project, minor project, hackathon, and more. We'll take hackathon.

4
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:31.233
Give it a name, and the submission deadline. Karya lays out the usual steps, and dates each one back from that deadline.

5
00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:39.741
Every project has its own link. Share it on WhatsApp, and your teammates join straight away, even from other colleges.

6
00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:48.329
Here's the board. The steps are already there, each with a due date, and the countdown at the top shows how long you've got.

7
00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:54.733
Open a card, and give it to someone. They get a notification straight away.

8
00:00:57.520 --> 00:01:01.669
When a teammate moves a card, you see it straight away, with no reloading.

9
00:01:03.160 --> 00:01:06.827
Click GitHub in the project menu, and connect your repo in one click.

10
00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:18.916
Now, when someone opens an issue on GitHub, it lands on your board by itself. Close it on GitHub, and the card closes too. You can also click Fetch from GitHub, any time.

11
00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:28.976
The Team page shows who's doing what. To do, doing, and done. So there are no surprises, right before the viva.

12
00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:34.800
And Today shows every deadline, and all your tasks, across all your projects.

13
00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:41.287
That's Karya for students. It's free, for your whole team. Good luck with your project!
